    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are an AI assistant that evaluates job opportunities based on a user profile.\n\nYou are given structured job data extracted from an email.\n\n-----------------------------------\nINPUT DATA:\n\nJob Data:\n- isJobOrInternship: {{$json[\"output\"][\"isJobOrInternship\"]}}\n- company: {{$json[\"output\"][\"company\"]}}\n- role: {{$json[\"output\"][\"Role\"]}}\n- salary: {{$json[\"output\"][\"salary\"]}}\n- link: {{$json[\"output\"][\"link\"]}}\n- platformOrUser: {{$json[\"output\"][\"platformOrUser\"]}}\n- deadline: {{$json[\"output\"][\"deadline\"]}}\n- offerType: {{$json[\"output\"][\"offerType\"]}}\n\n-----------------------------------\nUSER PROFILE:\n\nResume:\nEducation\nB.Tech – Computer Science and Engineering Jun 2022 – Jul 2026\nNarula Institute of Technology, West Bengal — CGPA: 9.14\nRelevant Coursework: DSA, OS, DBMS, CN, OOP, ML, AI, Software Engineering\nClass XII – CBSE 2021\nHariyana Vidya Mandir, Kolkata — 82.67%\nClass X – CBSE 2019\nNarayana Schools, Kolkata — 82.5%\nAcademic Projects\nMachine Learning Systems & Web Deployments — Link Jun 2025 – Feb 2026\n• Built an independent fraud detection system on 6.3M+ financial transactions handling extreme class imbalance\n(0.13%) using Logistic Regression and Random Forest, achieving ROC-AUC 0.985 and F1-score 0.81.\n• Executed complete ML pipeline including data cleaning, EDA, feature engineering, multicollinearity analysis,\nand model evaluation using Precision–Recall metrics for imbalanced classification.\n• During Unified Mentor Internship (Jun 2025 – Jul 2025), developed and deployed 3 ML web applications using\nFlask integration: Car Price Predictor (R2=0.89), House Price Predictor (R2=0.83, RMSE 37.37K), and Phone\nPrice Classifier (F1=0.94).\nData Analytics & Business Intelligence Applications — Link Jan 2026\n• Built interactive Power BI dashboard analyzing 100,000+ e-commerce records to evaluate sales performance,\nprofitability, regional trends, and customer segments.\n• Designed 10 dynamic KPIs including YTD Sales, Profit, Quantity, and Profit Margin using DAX with unified\ndata modeling and cross-filtering enabled across all visuals.\n• Performed diagnostic analysis to identify revenue concentration in West and East regions, product-level sales\nimbalance, and improved profit margins despite declining sales volume.\nFederated Learning Research for Fraud Detection Dec 2025\n• Team project — led research on Federated Learning for privacy-preserving fraud detection in banking, analyzing\ndecentralized ML workflows and secure data-sharing constraints.\n• Contributed to system design, feasibility analysis, and documentation outlining real-world implementation for\ndistributed financial analytics.\nTechnical Skills\nProgramming: Python, Java, C, C++.\nAI & ML: Scikit-learn, Pandas, NumPy, Prompt Engineering\nData Tools: SQL, Power BI, Excel\nWeb Development: HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Bootstrap\nTools: Git/GitHub, Jupyter Notebook, VS Code, PyCharm\nCertifications & Achievements\n• Winner – IBM SkillsBuild CSRBOX Winter Certification Program: Developed an AI-powered marketing model\nusing prompt engineering, sentiment analysis (Watson AI), and generative AI tools for end-to-end product launch\nsimulation. — Link\n• 4\nth Rank – Hack-O-NIT Hackathon: Contributed to solution design and presented an AI-based yoga posture\ndetection system providing real-time corrective feedback.\n• NPTEL Certifications – Artificial Intelligence: Search Methods for Problem Solving, Soft Computing.\n• 5-Star Gold Badge – Python, SQL, Java, Problem Solving (HackerRank).\n\n\n\n\nPreferences:\n- Preferred Roles: Software Developer, Data Analyst\n- Minimum Salary: 4 LPA\n- Graduation Year: 2026\n\n-----------------------------------\nEVALUATION RULES:\n\n1. Reject if:\n   - isJobOrInternship = false\n   - link is null\n   - role is unclear or too generic\n   - email is promotional or indirect\n\n2. Role Matching:\n   - Prefer roles: Software Developer, Data Analyst\n   - Allow closely related roles (e.g., Backend Developer, ML Engineer, Data Science Intern)\n\n-----------------------------------\nSALARY & OFFER TYPE LOGIC:\n\nA. For JOBS:\n   - If salary is provided:\n       → Accept ONLY if salary >= 4 LPA\n       → If salary < 4 LPA → mark isRelevant = false\n   - If salary is null:\n       → Do NOT reject, but reduce match_score\n\nB. For INTERNSHIPS:\n   - Accept ALL internships (stipend or unpaid)\n   - Do NOT reject based on salary/stipend\n   - Still check role relevance\n\n-----------------------------------\nADDITIONAL RULES:\n\n3. Fresher Eligibility:\n   - Prefer roles suitable for 2026 graduates\n\n4. Deadline Handling:\n   - If deadline is in the past → mark isRelevant = false\n\n-----------------------------------\nSCORING LOGIC:\n\n- Start from 0\n- Add based on:\n  - Role match\n  - Skill alignment (Python, ML, SQL, Web)\n  - Fresher eligibility\n  - Salary fit (ONLY for jobs)\n- Final match_score: 0–100\n\n-----------------------------------\nOUTPUT RULES:\n\n- Return ONLY valid JSON\n- Do NOT add extra text\n- Keep explanation short and precise (1–2 lines)\n\n-----------------------------------\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\n\n{\n  \"isJobOrInternship\": \"\",\n  \"company\": \"\",\n  \"role\": \"\",\n  \"salary\": \"\",\n  \"link\": \"\",\n  \"platformOrUser\": \"\",\n  \"deadline\": \"\",\n  \"offerType\": \"\",\n  \"isRelevant\": \"\",\n  \"reason\": \"\",\n  \"match_score\": \"\"\n}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {}
      },
